{"availability":"available","full":"xarantolus/ax","name":"ax","description":"Minimal x86-64 emulator for WebAssembly - run ELF binaries in your browser","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":90,"forks":7,"created":"2022-09-13T09:52:55Z","updated":"2024-03-25T22:25:26Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ax.010.one","topics":["ax-x86","elf","npm-package","rust","webassembly","x86","x86-64","x86-64-emulator","x86-emulator"],"demo":"https://ax.010.one/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T16:12:34.527Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T16:12:34.527Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T16:12:34.527Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T14:33:18.944Z","stars":90,"forks":7},{"at":"2026-10-04T16:12:34.527Z","stars":90,"forks":7}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is a minimal x86-64 emulator for WebAssembly. It executes real machine code and can be used to emulate x86-64 user-space programs in the browser.","Currently implemented are 315 opcodes for 65 mnemonics (37 complete, 28 partial), which is only a very small subset of the more than 981 available mnemonics with at least 3684 variants Source. More detailed stats can be found via the stats.py script.","Note that not all implemented instructions work exactly the same way as on real hardware, but the goal is to be as close as possible while staying reasonable. Notable exceptions are instructions that interact with the operating system (interrupts, syscalls) and the omission of all flags that are not used by jump instructions."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/xarantolus/ax/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8ef61a6ff9c1b6b532c8f2b13f6e09dd935d0b831c8fbe957b59b0b8fdf0e059","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:27:06.534Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:19.313Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2024-03-25T22:25:26Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:19.315Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This is a minimal